p.src:
Newton did not obtain the inverse-square dependence from dimensional analysis. Kepler’s planetary laws supplied the decisive clue. For a circular orbit of radius $r$ and angular frequency $\omega$, $a_{\mathrm{circ}}=\omega^2r.$ If the acceleration caused by gravity varies as $1/r^2$, then $\omega^2r\propto\frac1{r^2}
  \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
  \omega^2\propto\frac1{r^3}.$ Since $T=2\pi/\omega$, $\boxed{T^2\propto r^3,}$ which is Kepler’s period–radius law. The same inverse-square force also produces elliptical, not merely circular, bound orbits.

