For many particles, let $\vec r_i$ and $m_i$ be the position and mass of particle $i$. Define $\vec r_{ij}=\vec r_j-\vec r_i$, the vector pointing from $i$ to $j$. The force on $i$ is then $\vec F_i
  =
  \sum_{j\ne i}
  Gm_im_j
  \frac{\vec r_j-\vec r_i}
       {|\vec r_j-\vec r_i|^3}.$ Every term points toward its source. The lecture’s temporary minus-sign confusion is only a choice between $\vec r_{ij}$ and $\vec r_{ji}=-\vec r_{ij}$; once the displacement vector is defined, the sign is fixed.

