p.src:
Substitution into $m_i\vec a_i=\vec F_i$ cancels the mass of the body whose motion is being followed: $\boxed{
  \vec a_i
  =
  \sum_{j\ne i}
  Gm_j
  \frac{\vec r_j-\vec r_i}
       {|\vec r_j-\vec r_i|^3}.}$ The acceleration depends on all the source masses but not on $m_i$. Universality of free fall survives the move from uniform gravity to the full Newtonian field.

