p.src:
After the break we need one piece of vector calculus. For a generic vector field $\vec A=(A_x,A_y,A_z)$, define $\boxed{
  \nabla\cdot\vec A
  =
  \frac{\partial A_x}{\partial x}
  +\frac{\partial A_y}{\partial y}
  +\frac{\partial A_z}{\partial z}.}$ The upside-down triangle, $\nabla$, represents the three spatial derivatives. Although it acts on a vector field, the dot product leaves a scalar.

